  "body": "Main is red since `81407b31b` (merge of PR #2894, issue #2887). Two PRs that were each green on their own now disagree:\n\n- PR #2024 (issue #1700, merged at `3ffe2338f`) added `crates/app/tests/stock_source_holes.rs` with `framed_stock_chamfer_live_refusal_keeps_hint_without_local_move_number`.\n- PR #2894 (merged at `81407b31b`) refuses a 2D Chamfer with no picks on an edge loop that is only partly bevelled.\n\nReproduced on `81407b31b` (Linux; also red in the m3 macOS check):\n\n```\npanicked at crates/app/tests/stock_source_holes_support/mod.rs:260:58:\ngenerate: MachiningAt { msg: \"S1: invalid machining parameters: the edge loop near X35.000 Y20.249 carries a modelled chamfer on only part of its length - it is sharp near X-35.000 Y-16.176 - a chamfer with no picks would cut the sharp part; pick the edges to break\", at: Point3 { x: -18.378, y: 35.0, z: 12.379 } }\n```\n\nThe fixture's setup now meets #2894's refusal before the refusal the test expects (the live stock-source hint).\n\nTo decide: if the fixture loop really is only partly chamfered, the refusal is correct and the fixture (or its picks) changes, so the test still reaches the stock-source refusal it pins. If the loop is fully chamfered and #2894 reads it as partial, that is a defect in #2894's check (then P1: a correct chamfer is refused, and the reading of the model is wrong).\n\nDone means: the test passes on main, and the reason (fixture change or #2894 fix) is recorded on this issue.\n",
